# production_profile.config — debug-off fragment for Phase 6 / release builds.
#
# This fragment is one half of an explicit **two-profile** posture for the
# OnePlus 15 (infiniti) kernel:
#
#   DEVELOPMENT PROFILE — the base defconfig + gki_defconfig + canoe_perf
#     fragments WITHOUT this file merged. Carries KASAN, UBSAN, SLUB_DEBUG,
#     and RANDOMIZE_KSTACK_OFFSET so memory-safety bugs surface at boot/
#     operation time during bring-up. This is the default for CI and local
#     development.
#
#   PRODUCTION PROFILE — same base, plus this fragment merged on top.
#     Disables the four debug instrumentation classes so kernel struct
#     layouts and compiler-attribute annotations converge with OEM's
#     production-config kernel. The flashable Phase 6 ROM uses this profile
#     so OEM-prebuilt vendor modules can load via the canonical KMI
#     mechanism rather than rebuild-everything-from-source.
#
# NEITHER profile is "more correct." Development profile catches bugs that
# production profile silently absorbs; production profile carries CRCs that
# OEM modules can interoperate with. Pick deliberately per build.
#
# DO NOT delete this fragment when switching back to development profile —
# remove it from TARGET_KERNEL_CONFIG in BoardConfigCommon.mk instead.
# Keeping the file in tree preserves the dual-profile capability without
# requiring the next agent to reconstruct it.
#
# ===========================================================================
# Background (Phase 2.5 KMI-strict audit, 2026-05-11)
# ===========================================================================
#
# Authored to test the hypothesis that debug-config divergence (KASAN,
# UBSAN, SLUB_DEBUG, RANDOMIZE_KSTACK_OFFSET) drove the OEM-prebuilt CRC
# divergence found in the KMI-strict audit. The first audit measured
# 557/557 OEM vendor_dlkm modules fail `module_layout` CRC.
#
# Empirical result (re-audit after merging this fragment):
# **ZERO convergence.** Disabling these debug configs produced NO change
# to OEM-prebuilt-load-fail counts. CRCs of foundational kernel APIs
# (`_printk`, `module_layout`, `mutex_lock`, `kfree`, etc.) were
# UNCHANGED by the flips, confirming these CONFIGs only affect
# instrumentation symbols (`kasan_flag_enabled`, etc.) but NOT struct
# layouts or signatures visible to genksyms.
#
# The divergence cause is **kernel-source / ACK patch-level skew** —
# OEM `android16-5-o-g362117606264` vs our `android16-6.12-2025-06_r8`.
# Cannot be fixed by config flips. Path B (full source-build of the
# OEM corpus) is the only path forward; targeted whitelist extensions
# can address the load-fail-missing cohort but not the load-fail-crc
# cohort which dominates.
#
# This fragment is preserved in tree as a documented production-debug-off
# option (e.g., for perf measurement or KASAN-overhead-zero builds), NOT
# as part of the KMI-alignment strategy. To use: append
# `production_profile.config` to TARGET_KERNEL_CONFIG in
# device/oneplus/sm8850-common/BoardConfigCommon.mk. Note: source-built
# modules will then need to be rebuilt against the new kernel
# Module.symvers; the depmod step will fail if source-built consumers
# of KASAN symbols (e.g., msm_gpi.ko, qca_cld3_*) still carry stale
# `__versions` from a KASAN-on build.
#
# See kmi_strict_audit.md "Path B' result" and IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md
# §2.5 for the empirical evidence trail.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CONFIG_SLUB_DEBUG
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Adds redzone + freelist debug fields to struct kmem_cache. Affects CRCs
# for every consumer of kfree / kmalloc_caches / __kmalloc_* / devm_kmalloc.
# Boot-time: validates allocator metadata; can catch use-after-free and
# double-free bugs early. Production builds skip it for perf + struct-
# layout-stability.
# CONFIG_SLUB_DEBUG is not set

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CONFIG_UBSAN — Undefined Behavior Sanitizer
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Compiler instruments potentially-undefined-behavior expressions (signed
# overflow, OOB array index, null deref, etc.) with runtime checks. Adds
# attribute annotations to instrumented function symbols that affect their
# genksyms CRCs. CONFIG_UBSAN_TRAP / _BOUNDS / _ARRAY_BOUNDS / _LOCAL_BOUNDS
# auto-disable when CONFIG_UBSAN=n.
# CONFIG_UBSAN is not set

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CONFIG_KASAN — Kernel Address Sanitizer
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Hardware-tagged-memory sanitizer (HW_TAGS mode requires ARMv8.5 MTE).
# Affects compiler attribute annotations on instrumented symbols even
# though HW_TAGS doesn't add as much struct-layout drift as GENERIC mode.
# CONFIG_KASAN_HW_TAGS and CONFIG_KASAN_VMALLOC auto-disable when
# CONFIG_KASAN=n.
# CONFIG_KASAN is not set

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CONFIG_RANDOMIZE_KSTACK_OFFSET
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Randomizes kernel stack offset per system call entry. Affects the
# `__stack_chk_fail` symbol's CRC because stack-canary placement and
# checking are entangled. OEM uses static canary placement; matching
# their behavior converges the symbol.
# CONFIG_RANDOMIZE_KSTACK_OFFSET is not set

# ===========================================================================
# Path B'' additions (2026-05-11) — comprehensive flip list
# ===========================================================================
#
# After v1 (the 4 flags above) produced zero CRC convergence, Path B''
# expands the flip set to comprehensively test all CRC-affecting CONFIGs
# that differ between our dev profile and OEM's deduced production
# profile. Each entry below names a flag, our evidence for OEM's value,
# and the suspected CRC-affect mechanism.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CONFIG_CFI_CLANG — Control Flow Integrity (Clang)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HIGH leverage. Direct empirical evidence: 5/5 randomly sampled OEM
# .ko files have 0 `__cfi_check` symbols and 0 CFI ELF sections.
# OEM kernel definitively has CFI OFF. Our build has =y.
# CRC mechanism: CFI adds type-signature hashes to indirect function
# calls, materializing in struct definitions that carry function-pointer
# fields. Any struct with a `function_pointer_t` member gets a CFI
# annotation when CFI is on, shifting genksyms CRC.
# CONFIG_CFI_CLANG is not set

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CONFIG_LIST_HARDENED
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HIGH leverage. Hardens list-manipulation primitives (list_add,
# list_del). Source of `__list_add_valid_or_report`, which 116 OEM
# boot-loaded modules consume. If OEM has it off, the function and its
# CRC shift dramatically.
# CONFIG_LIST_HARDENED is not set

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CONFIG_SLAB_FREELIST_HARDENED
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Adds freelist-pointer obfuscation in struct kmem_cache. Affects slab
# allocator function CRCs.
# CONFIG_SLAB_FREELIST_HARDENED is not set

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CONFIG_HARDENED_USERCOPY
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Adds runtime bounds checks to copy_to_user / copy_from_user. May
# affect struct usercopy_region descriptors and copy primitive
# signatures.
# CONFIG_HARDENED_USERCOPY is not set

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CONFIG_DEBUG_KERNEL — umbrella
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Master switch enabling many debug sub-options. Production kernels
# typically have this off. Disabling cascade-disables others.
# CONFIG_DEBUG_KERNEL is not set

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_BTF / _BTF_MODULES
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generates BTF (BPF Type Format) information for in-kernel types.
# Doesn't directly affect Module.symvers CRCs (BTF is a separate ELF
# section) but flip-tested for completeness.
# CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_BTF is not set
# CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_BTF_MODULES is not set

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CONFIG_KFENCE — KASAN-class allocator sampling
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Probabilistic memory-safety check (samples allocations). Adds fields
# to slab metadata. Production kernels typically don't ship it.
# CONFIG_KFENCE is not set

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CONFIG_KUNIT — kernel unit-test framework
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Unit tests. OEM almost certainly doesn't ship it. Probably no CRC
# effect on non-test modules; flipped for completeness.
# CONFIG_KUNIT is not set

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CONFIG_INIT_STACK_ALL_ZERO
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Stack-local-variable zero-init. Compiler attribute, unlikely to
# affect Module.symvers CRCs but flipped for completeness.
# CONFIG_INIT_STACK_ALL_ZERO is not set
